  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, tells of Itzhak Bentov, an inventor and author of the book Stalking the Wild Pendulum. Michels says Bentov's theories helped lay the groundwork for the Gateway Process, a method for altering consciousness developed by the researcher Robert Monroe in Virginia and studied by the CIA, the US spy agency, and for its psychic spying work. If true, it would mean fringe ideas about consciousness shaped real intelligence programmes."
